# Secrets. The Anthropic API key is not read at runtime — the Makefile bakes it
# into the kernel with -DTALKOS_API_KEY='"$(KEY)"'. So the key leaks from more
# than the .env it is kept in:
#
#   .env           where the key is kept (os/.env, appliance/.env)
#   .build-flags   the stamp that forces a rebuild when KEY changes. It records
#                  the flag set verbatim, i.e. the literal `KEY=sk-ant-...`
#
# Every other artifact the key ends up inside (*.o, kernel.elf, kernel.bin,
# talkos.iso, os/build/) is ignored under "Build artifacts" below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.build-flags

# Build artifacts
*.o
kernel.elf
kernel.bin

# Dependency files from the compiler's -MMD -MP, one per object
*.d

# Host test binaries from `make test-host`. Leading **/ because a pattern with a
# slash in it is anchored to this file's directory, and the tree is os/tests/.
**/tests/build/

# Packet capture from `make run-pcap`
net.pcap

# Bootable media from `make iso` (a 4 MB ISO and its staging tree)
talkos.iso
os/build/

# Scratch idea notes
ideas/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Appliance (Python)
appliance/.venv/
appliance/visual_check.png
__pycache__/
*.pyc
